---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
import SvgDefs from "../components/SvgDefs.astro"
import ThemeToggle from "../components/ThemeToggle.astro"
import { loginUrl } from "../lib/config"

const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    name: "Sealed scratchpads",
    url: new URL("/encryption", Astro.site).href,
    about: "End-to-end encrypted scratchpads in Threa, for work with your own coding agent.",
  },
]
---

<Layout
  title="Sealed scratchpads · Threa"
  description="A sealed scratchpad is end-to-end encrypted: messages, agent replies, trace steps and even the name are encrypted on your devices, and Threa's servers hold ciphertext. For the work you do with your own coding agent."
  schema={schema}
>
  <SvgDefs />

  <!-- ============================================================
       HERO — the premise, stated for someone who has never read the
       crypto page. Same masthead as /about.
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="frame">
    <div class="hero-shell">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="nav-row" data-decorative>
          <div class="brand">
            <svg><use href="#threa-mark" /></svg>
            <span class="wordmark">Threa</span>
          </div>
          <nav class="nav-links">
            <a href="/">Product</a>
            <a href="/about">About</a>
            <a href="/developers">Developers</a>
          </nav>
          <a class="nav-login" href={loginUrl}>Log in</a>
          <ThemeToggle />
        </div>

        <div class="enc-hero">
          <h1 class="h-display">
            Some of it should<br />
            stay between you<br />
            and your agent.
          </h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Working with your own coding agent means pasting commands, diffs and
            output you would not paste into a group chat. A sealed scratchpad
            encrypts all of it on your devices. Threa's servers hold the
            ciphertext and have no way to open it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       01 · WHAT IS SEALED. Three open columns, no cards.
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="frame warm">
    <div class="memo-shell">
      <h2>What the server never sees.</h2>
      <p class="lede enc-lede">
        Encryption covers scratchpads and the threads under them. The key is
        yours. Everything written in one is encrypted in your browser, or on the
        machine your agent runs on, before it is sent.
      </p>

      <div class="enc-duo">
        <div class="enc-q">
          <h3>The conversation</h3>
          <p>
            Your messages, the agent's replies, and every trace step it writes
            while it works. The command it ran and what came back are in the
            stream where you can read them, and nowhere else.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="enc-q">
          <h3>Even the name</h3>
          <p>
            The title is encrypted too, and your browser decrypts it for the
            sidebar. A list of your scratchpads gives away nothing about what is
            in them. Threa names the others for you by reading them. This one you
            name yourself.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="enc-q">
          <h3>Its questions</h3>
          <p>
            When the agent stops to ask whether to run the migration, the
            question, the choices and the note you type back are sealed. The
            server learns which option you picked, because it has to check the
            answer is one of the ones on offer.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       02 · HOW IT WORKS. Three steps in plain order.
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="frame">
    <div class="memo-shell">
      <h2>One passphrase, then it's on.</h2>

      <ol class="enc-steps">
        <li>
          <h3>Set up encryption once</h3>
          <p>
            Under Settings, in the AI tab. You pick a passphrase, and it wraps a
            key that never leaves your device unwrapped. Unlock on each device you
            use, or keep that device unlocked with a PIN or your fingerprint.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Let your agent in</h3>
          <p>
            Invite the bot from the scratchpad's header and Threa wraps the
            scratchpad's key to the key on that machine. Take it back out and the
            wraps it could open are deleted and the key rolls forward: it keeps
            what it already read and gets nothing sent after.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Read it from the terminal</h3>
          <p>
            <code>threa e2e unlock</code> once puts your key in the OS keychain.
            After that the ordinary commands work on a sealed scratchpad the way
            they work anywhere else: <code>threa streams read</code> prints it,
            <code>threa messages send</code> posts to it. The terminal does the
            encrypting, so an agent with a shell needs nothing else.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="enc-cta-row">
        <a class="os-cta" href="/developers/recipes#sealed-agent">Connect an encrypted agent</a>
        <a class="os-cta" href="/developers/cli#e2e">Read one from the CLI</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       03 · THE TRADE. Say the cost out loud, before someone finds it.
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="frame warm">
    <div class="memo-shell">
      <h2>What it costs.</h2>
      <p class="lede enc-built-lede">
        Anything Threa does by reading your messages stops at the seal. Nothing
        in a sealed scratchpad is searchable and nothing in one becomes a memo,
        so the knowledge base Threa builds from your conversations skips it.
        Scheduled messages and stream briefs are off there for the same reason.
      </p>
      <p class="lede enc-built-lede">
        Lose the passphrase and that content is gone for good. There is no reset,
        because a reset would mean someone else had a copy of the key. That is the
        whole point, and it is worth knowing before you turn it on.
      </p>
      <p class="lede enc-built-lede">
        Everything outside sealed scratchpads works the usual way. Channels, DMs
        and threads are encrypted in transit and at rest like any other service,
        and Threa can read them, which is how search and memory work at all.
        Encryption is for the scratchpads where you and your agent do the work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       CLOSE
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="frame">
    <div class="memo-shell is-centerpiece enc-close">
      <h2>Open, and checkable.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        The crypto is RFC 9180 HPKE with AES-256-GCM, and the code that does it is
        in the public repo. Read it before you trust it.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="cta" href="/#waitlist">Join the waitlist</a>
        <a class="os-cta" href="https://github.com/threahq/threa">Read the source</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="brand" style="gap:10px;">
      <svg style="width:24px;height:24px;color:hsl(var(--gold));"><use href="#threa-mark" /></svg>
      <span class="wordmark" style="font-size:18px;">Threa</span>
      <span class="year">2026</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ln">
      <a href="/">Product</a>
      <a href="/about">About</a>
      <a href="/developers">Developers</a>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <style>
    /* Masthead: headline and framing side by side, same as /about. */
    .enc-hero {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
      gap: 56px;
      align-items: end;
    }
    .enc-hero .lede { max-width: 460px; font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 6px; }
    .enc-lede { max-width: 620px; font-size: 17px; margin: 0 0 4px; }

    .enc-duo {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 40px;
      margin-top: 24px;
    }
    .enc-q { border-top: 1px solid hsl(var(--line)); padding-top: 20px; }
    .enc-q h3,
    .enc-steps h3 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: 19px;
      line-height: 1.3;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
    }
    .enc-q p,
    .enc-steps p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: hsl(var(--ink-soft));
    }

    /* Numbered steps: the count sits in the gutter as a mono gold marker. */
    .enc-steps {
      list-style: none;
      counter-reset: enc-step;
      margin: 24px 0 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      gap: 26px;
      max-width: 640px;
    }
    .enc-steps li {
      counter-increment: enc-step;
      position: relative;
      padding-left: 40px;
    }
    .enc-steps li::before {
      content: counter(enc-step);
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      top: 1px;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12px;
      color: hsl(var(--gold));
    }
    .enc-steps code {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 13px;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
    }

    .enc-built-lede { max-width: 640px; font-size: 17px; }
    .enc-built-lede + .enc-built-lede { margin-top: 16px; }
    .enc-cta-row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 14px 28px;
      margin-top: 28px;
    }
    .enc-cta-row .os-cta { margin-top: 0; }
    .enc-close .actions {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 12px 18px;
      margin-top: 8px;
    }
    .enc-close .os-cta { margin-top: 0; }

    @media (max-width: 880px) {
      .enc-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; align-items: start; }
      .enc-duo { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
